# Paths cakebear owns.
#
# Everything else in this repository belongs to upstream
# (github.com/microsoft/typescript-go) and must not be modified outside an
# upstream sync. See CLAUDE.md, "The golden rule", for why.
#
# One path per line. A trailing slash means "this directory and everything
# under it"; anything else is an exact file path. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored.
#
# Deliberately extensionless: upstream's .gitignore has a blanket `*.txt` rule,
# so this file was silently untracked for five phases when it was called
# owned-paths. Adding a negation to .gitignore is not an option -- that is
# an upstream file. Do not give this a .txt extension.
#
# Read by:
#   scripts/check-upstream-untouched.sh  (fails a PR that touches upstream)
#   scripts/check-boundary.sh            (keeps ir/ and backend/ extractable)
#   scripts/check-line-limit.py          (only lints .go files we own)
#   scripts/owned-go-packages.sh         (test, coverage and lint scoping)
#   scripts/sync-upstream.sh             (refuses to auto-resolve our files)

cmd/cakec/
ir/
lower/
backend/
types/
examples/
scripts/
CLAUDE.md
README.md
.github/workflows/cakebear-ci.yml
.github/workflows/cakebear-sync-upstream.yml
